// Chapter — a saga chapter ability as data [CR#714.2b]: "{rN}—[Effect]"
// means "When one or more lore counters are put onto this Saga, if the
// number of lore counters on it was less than N and became at least N,
// [effect]." `OneOrMore` matches the placement BATCH once ([CR#603.3b]),
// and `Crossed` is [CR#714.2b]'s was-less-than/became-at-least gate
// verbatim, read off the fired fact's before/after channel — a
// counter-doubled 0→2 jump is ONE fact whose crossing chapters I and II
// each observe (and chapter III does not). The Saga subtype registry row
// (types/enchantment/Saga.ron) confers the enters-with-counter Also
// [CR#714.3a] and the turn-based lore increment [CR#714.3c]; the
// final-chapter sacrifice SBA carries the card's own final chapter
// number, so it is spelled card-side ([CR#714.4,714.2d] — the Idris
// History of Benalia exemplar).
//
// The inner ability is `Innate` — the rule OF THE CHAPTER SYMBOL
// ([CR#714.2] "a chapter symbol is a keyword ability that represents a
// triggered ability"); removal strips the authored Expanded wrapper.
//
// Usage: Chapter(n: 2, effect: <chapter effect>).
(
    name: "Chapter",
    template: "${n} — ${effect}",
    kinds: [Ability],
    params: { "n": Count, "effect": Effect },
    body: Innate(Triggered(
        event: OneOrMore(CounterPlaced(kind: LoreCounter, on: Ref(This))),
        condition: Crossed(
            value: CounterCount(This, LoreCounter),
            threshold: AtLeast(Param(n)),
        ),
        effect: Param(effect),
    )),
)
